From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <bap@debian.org>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: blowfish: fix 8-byte stack overflow in the self test

Forwarded: no

blowfish_selftest() sets up the IV for each of the six chained-mode
tests with

	memcpy(block, IV, 16);

but both IV and block are uint8_t[8] -- Blowfish has a 64-bit block,
so an 8-byte IV is the only size that makes sense here.  The copy
therefore reads 8 bytes past the end of IV and writes 8 bytes past the
end of block, into whatever follows it on the stack (in practice buf[],
which is overwritten immediately afterwards, which is why this has gone
unnoticed).

It is still undefined behaviour, and with _FORTIFY_SOURCE it is the
kind of thing that turns into a runtime abort when the compiler stops
being able to prove otherwise.  gcc already sees it:

  In function 'memcpy',
      inlined from 'blowfish_selftest' at blowfish.c:537:2:
  /usr/include/x86_64-linux-gnu/bits/string_fortified.h:29:10: warning:
    '__builtin___memcpy_chk' forming offset [8, 15] is out of the bounds
    [0, 8] of object 'block' with type 'uint8_t[8]' [-Warray-bounds=]

Use sizeof(IV), which is what was meant.
---
 src/blowfish/blowfish.c | 12 ++++++------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/blowfish/blowfish.c b/src/blowfish/blowfish.c
index 144b1e8..75b74d8 100644
--- a/src/blowfish/blowfish.c
+++ b/src/blowfish/blowfish.c
@@ -534,32 +534,32 @@ blowfish_selftest(void)
 
 	blowfish_init(B, K, 16);
 
-	memcpy(block, IV, 16);
+	memcpy(block, IV, sizeof(IV));
 	blowfish_encrypt_cbc(B, block, P_cbc, buf, sizeof P_cbc);
 	if (memcmp(buf, C_cbc, sizeof C_cbc) != 0)
 		return -1;
 
-	memcpy(block, IV, 16);
+	memcpy(block, IV, sizeof(IV));
 	blowfish_decrypt_cbc(B, block, C_cbc, buf, sizeof P_cbc);
 	if (memcmp(buf, P_cbc, sizeof P_cbc) != 0)
 		return -1;
 
-	memcpy(block, IV, 16);
+	memcpy(block, IV, sizeof(IV));
 	blowfish_encrypt_cfb64(B, block, 0, P, buf, sizeof P);
 	if (memcmp(buf, C_cfb64, sizeof C_cfb64) != 0)
 		return -1;
 
-	memcpy(block, IV, 16);
+	memcpy(block, IV, sizeof(IV));
 	blowfish_decrypt_cfb64(B, block, 0, C_cfb64, buf, sizeof P);
 	if (memcmp(buf, P, sizeof P) != 0)
 		return -1;
 
-	memcpy(block, IV, 16);
+	memcpy(block, IV, sizeof(IV));
 	blowfish_encrypt_ofb64(B, block, 0, P, buf, sizeof P);
 	if (memcmp(buf, C_ofb64, sizeof C_ofb64) != 0)
 		return -1;
 
-	memcpy(block, IV, 16);
+	memcpy(block, IV, sizeof(IV));
 	blowfish_decrypt_ofb64(B, block, 0, C_ofb64, buf, sizeof P);
 	if (memcmp(buf, P, sizeof P) != 0)
 		return -1;
